ms":{"type":"number"},"minItems":3,"maxItems":3,"description":"[x, y, z] (cm)"},"direction":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"number"},"minItems":3,"maxItems":3,"description":"[x, y, z] (cm)"}}},"description":"Where roads join it."}},"description":"The ring and one exit per arm, in the order of toward."}},"required":["returnValue"]},"undoable":true,"irreversible":false,"requires_world":true,"async":false}]},"fluid":{"name":"fluid","version":"1.0.0","description":"Real-time fluid simulation (FluidNinja LIVE) on a 2D GPU grid: water (lakes, pools, seas) that ripples and wakes around\nanything moving through it; fire (bonfire, campfire, candle, flamethrower), smoke (columns, heavy smoke, explosions),\nfog / mist banks, mud and blood, snow and sand that keep tracks, drifting snow and sand, lava; plus flow sources (hoses,\njets, vortices, emitters) that push and feed simulations, and ambient particles (blizzard, sandstorm, rain, sparks).\nCharacters, vehicles and objects that generate overlap events disturb a simulation anywhere over its area (built\nmeshes do not by default); the fluid does not push objects back. Fog / mist turns on the level's volumetric fog.\nWorkflow: list (presets, effects, sources, ambient, what exists) -> add (a preset or effect at a place; size, yaw) ->\nadd_source to feed or stir it -> ambient for atmosphere -> screenshot -> remove. Pairs with sky.set_weather and\nsky.set_ground.","tools":[{"name":"add","function":"Add","description":"Adds a fluid simulation from a preset: the simulation plus the water surface it drives. Undoable.\nReturns: The new simulation. Fails if FluidNinja is not in the project, the preset or material is unknown, or a value is out of range.","input_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"preset":{"type":"string","description":"an effect: bonfire | fire | candle | smoke_column | heavy_smoke | explosion | flamethrower | magic | mist | mud | blood | snow_trails | snow_drift | sand_trails | sandstorm | lava (see list `effects`); shore water: coast_water (waves and whitewater rolling onto a beach; its sea level is always z = -480: build the ground with sea_level -480; reads the ground's height itself) | coast_sand (wet sand with footprints on the ground under it); or water: lake | pool | sea | sea_wavy | sea_200m | sea_wavy_200m | river | river_whitewater | river_whitewater_inverse | water_tank | tracks | default (or a preset asset path). Lakes, pools and seas look right anywhere (put ground below them, e.g. a terrain basin); the river presets are made to follow a spline over a landscape and look like a sandy bed with streaks on open ground."},"location":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"number"},"minItems":3,"maxItems":3,"description":"Centre of the area on the water level (cm), e.g. [0, 0, 20]. ([x, y, z] (cm))"},"size_meters":{"type":"number","description":"Side of the simulated square in metres, e.g. 80 (the preset's own size when omitted)."},"resolution":{"type":"integer","description":"Grid cells per side, 256-2048 (higher = finer ripples, more GPU), e.g. 1024."},"material":{"type":"string","description":"Water material, a short name from list `water_materials` (e.g. \"MI_Water_Quiet\") or a path."},"name":{"type":"string","description":"Node name, e.g. \"Lake\"."},"yaw":{"type":"number","description":"Turn the whole effect around its vertical axis, degrees (fire and smoke face the camera anyway)."},"follow_player":{"type":"boolean","description":"The simulation travels with the player's character (a beach, sea or sand area that is always around them, like the pack's coast demo); create the character first.","default":false},"ground":{"type":"string","description":"How the water reads the ground under it (shallows, shore waves): auto (a Landscape when the level has one, otherwise a top-down capture of whatever is there), landscape, capture, or flat.","default":"auto"}},"required":["preset"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":{"type":"object","properties":{"returnValue":{"t